# Anselm's Ontological Argument (Proslogion, Chapter II, ~1078 AD)
#
# God is defined as "that than which nothing greater can be conceived."
#
# Reductio: suppose God does not exist in reality, only in the understanding
# (in intellectu). Then God existing also in reality, IDEA(GOD)∧REALITY(GOD),
# is conceivable and greater than IDEA(GOD). But nothing
# conceivable is greater than God. So the supposition is false: God exists in
# reality (in re).
#
# The reductio is contraposition, from lib/logic.btp: from ⊢(¬R=>G) (premise 2)
# thCP gives ⊢(¬G=>R), and premise 1 is ⊢¬G.

<?py load('lib/logic.btp') ?>
## Terms
rTmGod   : GOD
rIdea    : IDEA(x)    # x exists in the understanding (in intellectu)
rReality : REALITY(x) # x exists in reality (in re)
rTmGt    : GT(x, y)   # x is greater than y

# Premises

## (1) Nothing conceivable is greater than God
rGodGreatest : ⊢¬GT(x, IDEA(GOD))

## (2) If x does not exist in reality, x existing also in reality is greater
rRealGreater : ⊢(¬REALITY(x)=>GT((IDEA(x)∧REALITY(x)), IDEA(x)))

# Proof

tmGod!           : rTmGod
tmGodIdea!       : rIdea x=tmGod!
tmGodReality!    : rReality x=tmGod!
tmGodAndReality! : rTmAnd p=tmGodIdea!;q=tmGodReality!
tmG!             : rTmGt x=tmGodAndReality!;y=tmGodIdea!    # G = GT((IDEA(GOD)∧REALITY(GOD)), IDEA(GOD))
tm¬G!            : rTmNeg p=tmG!
tm¬R!            : rTmNeg p=tmGodReality!                   # R = REALITY(GOD)
tm(¬R=>G)!       : rTmImp p=tm¬R!;q=tmG!
tm(¬G=>R)!       : rTmImp p=tm¬G!;q=tmGodReality!

## Suppose ¬R: then (IDEA(GOD)∧REALITY(GOD)) > IDEA(GOD), i.e. ¬R => G
thmRealGreater!  : rRealGreater x=tmGod!

## Contraposition: ¬G => R
thmCP!           : thCP i=tmGodReality!;j=tmG!
thmContraposed!  : rMp p=tm(¬R=>G)!;q=tm(¬G=>R)! thmRealGreater! thmCP!

## But nothing is greater than God: ¬G. So God exists in reality.
thmGreatest!     : rGodGreatest x=tmGodAndReality!
thmGodExistsInReality : rMp p=tm¬G!;q=tmGodReality! thmGreatest! thmContraposed!
